Founders struggle with the same depression that actors do; when the production is ready, who are you, really? In the limit of perfect imitation, you BECOME the character. Same founders - there is no 'after-work'! You ALWAYS work. If you don't, the competitor will and you will lose the market to them (mind, with some limitations). If you have VC acceleration, you have responsibility, and you feel the weight of their money on your sholders, and the opportunity cost if you don't. This is not to say that you LITERALLY always work; you need to care for your mortal vehicle, that stops obeying your commands to WORK MORE if you don't nurture it. You need to vent, eat, sleep. 

In this environment, the role you are playing as this central character, is a form of existence. Make one mistake, and this character will exist no more. Literally. 

if it fails, and it usually does, you need to have somthing to cling on to so you DON'T kill yourself - network, knowledge, skill, are usually things that you can acredit to yourself

